@startuml
Here is the UML state transition diagram in PlantUML format based on the given natural language requirement:

title Digidoclocker System States


[*] --> INITIAL_STATE : Citizen Registration Required

state "Initial State" as INITIAL_STATE {
  [*] --> REGISTRATION_REQUIRED : [citizen registration required]
}

state "Registration Required" as REGISTRATION_REQUIRED
REGISTRATION_REQUIRED : entry / citizen registration
REGISTRATION_REQUIRED : do / verify citizen details
REGISTRATION_REQUIRED : exit / successful registration


REGISTRATION_REQUIRED --> LOGGED_IN : [successful registration]

state "Logged In" as LOGGED_IN {
  [*] --> UPLOAD_DOCUMENTS : [citizen has uploaded documents]
}

state "Upload Documents" as UPLOAD_DOCUMENTS
UPLOAD_DOCUMENTS : entry / upload documents
UPLOAD_DOCUMENTS : do / view profile or apply for certificate
UPLOAD_DOCUMENTS : exit / continue uploading documents


LOGGED_IN --> VIEW_PROFILE_OR_APPLY_CERTIFICATE : [view profile or apply for certificate]

state "View Profile or Apply Certificate" as VIEW_PROFILE_OR_APPLY_CERTIFICATE {
  [*] --> APPLY_CERTIFICATE : [citizen has applied for a certificate]
}

state "Apply Certificate" as APPLY_CERTIFICATE
APPLY_CERTIFICATE : entry / apply for multiple certificates
APPLY_CERTIFICATE : do / reapply after sending request to issuer
APPLY_CERTIFICATE : exit / end session


VIEW_PROFILE_OR_APPLY_CERTIFICATE --> REGISTRAR_REQUEST_CERTIFICATE : [registrar requests certificate]

state "Registrar Request Certificate" as REGISTRAR_REQUEST_CERTIFICATE {
  [*] --> REQUEST_MULTIPLE_CERTIFICATES : [registrar has requested multiple certificates]
}

state "Request Multiple Certificates" as REQUEST_MULTIPLE_CERTIFICATES
REQUEST_MULTIPLE_CERTIFICATES : entry / request multiple certificates
REQUEST_MULTIPLE_CERTIFICATES : do / continue requesting more after receiving one
REQUEST_MULTIPLE_CERTIFICATES : exit / end session


REGISTRAR_REQUEST_CERTIFICATE --> END_SESSION : [end session]

state "End Session" as END_SESSION
END_SESSION : entry / end session

[*] --> REGISTRAR_REQUEST_CERTIFICATE : [registrar requests certificate]

This PlantUML code represents the Digidoclocker system states and transitions based on the given functional requirements. The initial state is `INITIAL_STATE`, where citizen registration is required. After successful registration, the system transitions to `LOGGED_IN` state. From there, citizens can upload documents or view their profile or apply for a certificate. Registrars can request certificates for verification. The session ends once the user is done with their actions.

Note that I have followed the PlantUML structural validation patterns and replaced placeholders with existing requirement-supported states, events, and guards.
@enduml
